{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109188","id":2712633487,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6hr4CP","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109188","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109188.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109188.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109188","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109188/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109188/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109188/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/fa36abeacc36049d71df03480081064b5f48f812","number":109188,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix FindClass() failing to find Dictionary on Android leading to crash","user":{"login":"limbonaut","id":2766569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NjY1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2766569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut","html_url":"https://github.com/limbonaut","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR fixes crashes that happen when you try to create an instance of a custom class using JNI (like `org.godotengine.godot.Dictionary`) from a non-main thread. The main issue is that FindClass has trouble finding such classes from a non-main thread. See explanation below.\r\n\r\nWe stumbled upon this problem while rolling out support for Android in the [Sentry SDK](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-godot) for Godot.\r\n\r\nPotentially, also fixes other cases of class not found like in JavaClassWrapper. I took the liberty to change other FindClass() call sites to use this safer class loader; however, let me know if you think we should be doing it selectively.\r\n\r\n- Resolves #109160\r\n\r\n## Issue explanation\r\nQuote from Android documentation:\r\n\r\n[FAQ: Why didn't FindClass find my class?](https://developer.android.com/training/articles/perf-jni#faq:-why-didnt-findclass-find-my-class)\r\n\r\n> You can get into trouble if you create a thread yourself (perhaps by calling pthread_create and then attaching it with AttachCurrentThread). Now there are no stack frames from your application. If you call FindClass from this thread, the JavaVM will start in the \"system\" class loader instead of the one associated with your application, so attempts to find app-specific classes will fail.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097562,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1NjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:android","name":"platform:android","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3MzE4Mjcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/crash","name":"crash","description":"","color":"885544","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id